<task>Resolve one concrete attempt to open this checked container.</task>
Character: {{ characterName | default('The player', true) }}
Container: {{ container.name }} — {{ container.description }}
Attempt: {{ containerOpenAction }}

Choose exactly one check. Use an unopposed check unless another character is directly and actively opposing the attempt.

Return only this XML. Use N/A when a skill or attribute does not apply. Use an empty <circumstanceModifiers/> when there are no modifiers.

For an unopposed check:
<containerOpenCheck>
  <type>unopposed</type>
  <reason>brief reason for this check and its difficulty</reason>
  <skill>exact skill name or N/A</skill>
  <attribute>exact attribute name or N/A</attribute>
  <difficultyLevel>Trivial|Easy|Medium|Hard|Very Hard|Legendary</difficultyLevel>
  <circumstanceModifiers>
    <modifier><amount>integer</amount><reason>brief reason</reason></modifier>
  </circumstanceModifiers>
</containerOpenCheck>

For an opposed check:
<containerOpenCheck>
  <type>opposed</type>
  <reason>brief reason for this opposed check</reason>
  <skill>exact acting character skill name or N/A</skill>
  <attribute>exact acting character attribute name or N/A</attribute>
  <opponent>exact opposing character name</opponent>
  <opponentSkill>exact skill name or N/A</opponentSkill>
  <opponentAttribute>exact attribute name or N/A</opponentAttribute>
  <circumstanceModifiers>
    <modifier><amount>integer</amount><reason>brief reason</reason></modifier>
  </circumstanceModifiers>
</containerOpenCheck>

{% llmparse('container_open_check_plan') as containerOpenCheck %}

The game has now resolved that check. This response is authoritative:
{{ containerOpenCheck.response }}

Do not choose another check and do not reroll.

State whether the result opens the container now, whether it permanently removes the check requirement, and what may be shown. Do not reveal contents on failure.

{% llm_dummy_action %}

Draft Response: Write brief visible prose for the attempt and exact check outcome without numerical stats or contents on failure. Output prose only.

{% llmparse('player_action_required_prose') %}

{% set tinyBrainAuditFocus = 'Exactly one check result is authoritative; success/permanentlyOpened must agree with it; a failure must not reveal contents; no reroll or extra tool result may be substituted.' %}
{% include "_includes/tinybrain-prose-audit.njk" %}

Did the successful result permanently remove this container's future check requirement? Answer yes or no. A failure must answer no.
{% llmparse('yes_no') as permanentlyOpened %}

Briefly explain how much in-world time the attempt consumed. Do not include a duration in this explanation.
{% llmparse('player_action_time_reasoning') as timeReasoning %}

State the exact elapsed duration only, rounded to the nearest minute, with a 1 minute minimum.
{% llmparse('player_action_duration', 1) as timeDuration %}

{% llmresult('container_open_result') %}
